    "decoder_context": [
      "Finite real Hilbert/Borel E with canonical volume, including0; NNReal are nonnegative reals. W/V are actual C2 potentials, not C-infinity. Both Hessian bounds are actual all-point/all-vector forms and source lower constant is positive.",
      "Measure.tilted(-W) is the true normalized exp(-W) Gibbs measure with actual positive integrable partition. MemLp/toLp and every norm are actual weighted L2 AE quotients. Original graph is exact compact-C-infinity classical gradient and genuine partial linear-map closure.",
      "Original D precedes every epsilon/f. The conclusion produces ONE actual u in D.closure.domain, its all-domain variational identity and all original local/ordinary weak/C2cutoff equations. No final cutoff norm limit, scalar inequality, core certificate or norm(x)*u moment is a premise.",
      "Generic scalar endpoint is m*norm(D.closureu)^2<=norm(f-epsilon*u)^2<=normf^2, with 0<m<=M. It does not assert epsilon-zero/Poincare/BL. Ordinary unlocalized innergradientW,G and PDE residual are only local; global weighted integrability is obtained after exact commutator cancellation.",
      "Source actual augmentation J and common Markov/disintegrating R/S are true Gaussian/reflected kernels. W_y=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), exact m=(alpha+eta^-1)/4 and M=(beta+eta^-1)/4; alpha/beta/eta cap retained. Auxiliary curvature kernels are not equated with resolvent kernels.",
