  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume; dimension zero is permitted and approved section instances are part of the contract. Let W:E->R be C2. Assume exp(-W) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. Let m,M be real numbers with 0<m and m<=M. Assume for every x,a:E BOTH actual all-point/all-vector curvature bounds\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a <= M*||a||^2.\nLet mu:Measure E be supplied with exact equality mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)), the actual normalized density exp(-W)/integral exp(-W) relative to volume.\nFor every real-linear partial operator D:L2(mu;R)->L2(mu;E), assume D.IsClosable and the exact original graph condition: for all scalar L2 a and vector L2 H, (a,H) belongs to D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real phi:E->R with a=phi mu-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) mu-almost everywhere. D.closure is the genuine same-graph closure operator on its submodule domain. This D is fixed before every epsilon/f.\nFor every real epsilon>0 and every f in L2(mu;R), there exists ONE u in D.closure.domain satisfying all the following simultaneous conclusions. Write u_rep,f_rep for standard measurable representatives of the actual scalar L2 classes, and G_rep for the standard representative of the actual vector class G=D.closure(u). Abbreviate the exact displayed ordinary PDE expression by r(x)=epsilon*u_rep(x)+<gradient(W)(x),G_rep(x)>_E-f_rep(x).\n(1) For every z in D.closure.domain,\n  epsilon*<u,z>_{L2(mu;R)}+<D.closure(u),D.closure(z)>_{L2(mu;E)}=<f,z>_{L2(mu;R)}.\n(2) u_rep and G_rep are locally integrable with respect to ordinary Lebesgue volume.\n(3) For every real C1 compactly supported psi and every direction a:E, both x->psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E and x->u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E dx = - integral u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\n(4) The real scalar function x->||r(x)||^2 is locally volume-integrable.\n(5) For every compact K:Set E, u_rep,G_rep,r each satisfy actual MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to volume.restrict K.\n(6) For every real C2 compactly supported q, both x->u_rep(x)*Delta(q)(x) and x->r(x)*q(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral u_rep(x)*Delta(q)(x) dx = integral r(x)*q(x) dx.\n(7) The following TWO global scalar inequalities hold for the actual weighted quotient classes:\n  m*||D.closure(u)||_{L2(mu;E)}^2 <= ||f-epsilon scalar-multiplied by u||_{L2(mu;R)}^2,\n  ||f-epsilon scalar-multiplied by u||_{L2(mu;R)}^2 <= ||f||_{L2(mu;R)}^2.\nHere f-epsilon*u is subtraction in the actual scalar L2 quotient, not an independently selected pointwise residual witness. It is distinct from the ordinary PDE expression r.\n(8) For every real C2 compactly supported chi, define the actual functions (v_chi denotes the statement's let-defined v)\n  v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x),\n  G_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by G_rep(x)+u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x),\n  F_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),G_rep(x)>_E+u_rep(x)*Delta(chi)(x).\nThen v_chi,G_chi,F_chi each satisfy actual global MemLp 2 volume, and each topological support is contained in tsupport(chi): tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(G_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(F_chi) subset tsupport(chi).\nFor every real C1 compactly supported psi and direction a:E, both x->psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nFor every real C2 compactly supported q, both x->v_chi(x)*Delta(q)(x) and x->F_chi(x)*q(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral v_chi(x)*Delta(q)(x) dx = integral F_chi(x)*q(x) dx.\nAll MemLp assertions mean actual a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm for their displayed measure. The ordinary local, compact-restricted and test assertions use canonical volume, whereas Hilbert inner products and both global inequalities use mu. Derivatives/Laplacians of potentials/tests/cutoffs are actual operators; no pointwise classical derivative or total Laplacian of the rough representative u is asserted. The same u/G serves all tests, all compact restrictions, both inequalities and ALL cutoffs. chi only has C2 and compact support; no range, positivity or plateau condition is added.\nThis is a universal implication for the supplied D, without an extra dense-domain premise or an existential D conclusion. W is C2, not assumed smooth of all orders. The positive lower bound and upper curvature bound are actual hypotheses here. The endpoint is global weighted scalar resolvent coercivity and the second norm bound for this epsilon>0 solution. No epsilon=0 theorem, characterization of the gradient kernel or constant-domain, centered/range or additional functional inequality, complete generator-adjoint/core/global Bochner identity, joint measurable selection, or kernel-cost/composition statement is asserted. In particular the stated global norm bounds do not separately assert global integrability of the ordinary pointwise inner product <gradient W,G_rep> or ordinary PDE residual r.",
